Found on k420. Apply::K8s::crd_get and the CRD GET in OCP::Drift both use the raw _request escape, with a comment that no IO::K8s class exists for CRDs. That is wrong: inside the image, IO::K8s 1.112 round-trips all four shipped CRDs without loss. Both reads must stay identical, so move them together to a typed get of CustomResourceDefinition, and drop them from the _request allow list in t/406. Lane: ocp-worker.

Cross-repo part not filed: Kubernetes::REST delete accepts only propagationPolicy, so the pod DELETE with gracePeriodSeconds in Apply/CR.pm stays on _request. The local kubernetes-rest clone points at an upstream without board write access; the card for the kubernetes-rest board (delete: accept gracePeriodSeconds) still has to be filed by the maintainer.

